We want to make it simple to log arbitrary user data. Currently, adding `AnyValues` in Rust and in C++ is very annoying. Now that we have eager-serialization this should be a lot simpler.

See also our docs: [https://rerun.io/docs/concepts/entity-component#adding-custom-data](https://rerun.io/docs/concepts/entity-component#adding-custom-data)

Supporting this use-case will likely become more important once we have recording properties with arbitrary data ([#9199](https://github.com/rerun-io/rerun/issues/9199)). Here is a comparison, with Python being the clear winner:

